Three improvements applied to `picoquictest_dualq.rs`:

1. **Removed `#![allow(non_upper_case_globals)]`** — this module has exactly one constant (`DUALQ_MAX_LINK_RATE`) which is already upper-case, so the allowance was covering nothing and would silently absorb future lint violations.

2. **`#[derive(Default)]` on `dualq_queue_t`** — `*mut T` implements `Default` (yielding `null_mut()`) in `core`, so the 23-line manual impl was pure boilerplate that `derive` handles identically.

3. **`#[derive(Default)]` on `dualq_state_t`** — same reasoning: every field type (`u64`, `i32`, `i64`, `f64`, and `dualq_queue_t` after change 2) satisfies `Default` with zero-value semantics, making the 30-line manual impl unnecessary.


